  {
   "id": "loop_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 176,
   "width": 604,
   "height": 90,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100006,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700042,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "loop:\n    seq   = bus.waitForNext(cursor)   # BUSY-SPIN, not a blocking wait\n    event = bus.read(seq)\n    process(event)                    # match, or update order state\n    bus.append(outboundEvents)\n    cursor = seq + 1",
   "originalText": "loop:\n    seq   = bus.waitForNext(cursor)   # BUSY-SPIN, not a blocking wait\n    event = bus.read(seq)\n    process(event)                    # match, or update order state\n    bus.append(outboundEvents)\n    cursor = seq + 1",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "loop",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "an",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 312,
   "width": 608,
   "height": 130,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100007,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700049,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "no locks              all critical-path state is touched by ONE thread. The\n                      concurrency control is the ABSENCE of concurrency.\nno context switches   a switch costs 1-10 us AND evicts cache. At a 30 us\n                      budget, one unlucky switch is a third of it.\nhot cache             the order books, the order index and the bus cursor\n                      all stay resident in L1/L2 on that core.\ndeterminism for free  one thread has ONE unambiguous execution order -\n                      which is exactly what replay needs.",
   "originalText": "no locks              all critical-path state is touched by ONE thread. The\n                      concurrency control is the ABSENCE of concurrency.\nno context switches   a switch costs 1-10 us AND evicts cache. At a 30 us\n                      budget, one unlucky switch is a third of it.\nhot cache             the order books, the order index and the bus cursor\n                      all stay resident in L1/L2 on that core.\ndeterminism for free  one thread has ONE unambiguous execution order -\n                      which is exactly what replay needs.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "an2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 456,
   "width": 568,
   "height": 81,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100008,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700056,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Busy-spinning rather than blocking: a blocking wait means a syscall to\nsleep, plus interrupt and scheduler latency to wake - 5 to 50 us of\nunpredictable delay. You are trading 100% of one CPU core for the\nelimination of wake-up latency. Absurd in most systems, obviously\ncorrect here.",
   "originalText": "Busy-spinning rather than blocking: a blocking wait means a syscall to\nsleep, plus interrupt and scheduler latency to wake - 5 to 50 us of\nunpredictable delay. You are trading 100% of one CPU core for the\nelimination of wake-up latency. Absurd in most systems, obviously\ncorrect here.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
