   "versionNonce": 700287,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "FUNCTIONAL   same inputs -> same outputs\nguaranteed by the sequencer plus pure matching",
   "originalText": "FUNCTIONAL   same inputs -> same outputs\nguaranteed by the sequencer plus pure matching",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "center",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "fd",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "ld",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 890,
   "y": 868,
   "width": 780,
   "height": 66,
   "strokeColor": "#b45309",
   "backgroundColor": "#fef3c7",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100042,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700294,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "ld_t",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ld_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 898,
   "y": 886,
   "width": 764,
   "height": 30,
   "strokeColor": "#374151",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100043,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700301,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "LATENCY   the same operation takes the same TIME, run to run\nguaranteed by NOTHING above - and this is what the tail requirement means",
   "originalText": "LATENCY   the same operation takes the same TIME, run to run\nguaranteed by NOTHING above - and this is what the tail requirement means",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "center",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "ld",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 950,
   "width": 1019,
   "height": 113,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100044,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700308,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Latency determinism's enemies are all systems-level: GC pauses, cache misses, page faults, interrupt handling, CPU frequency\nscaling, hyperthread contention, NUMA-remote memory. Mitigations are equally systems-level - isolcpus and IRQ affinity to keep\nother work off the core, huge pages, disabled frequency scaling and C-states, hyperthreading off on trading cores.\n\nWhich is why the measurement that matters is p99.99, not the mean. A system with a 5 us mean and a 2 ms p99.99 is UNUSABLE,\nbecause that 2 ms lands on somebody's order and costs them money. Functional determinism is correctness; latency determinism\nis the product.",
   "originalText": "Latency determinism's enemies are all systems-level: GC pauses, cache misses, page faults, interrupt handling, CPU frequency\nscaling, hyperthread contention, NUMA-remote memory. Mitigations are equally systems-level - isolcpus and IRQ affinity to keep\nother work off the core, huge pages, disabled frequency scaling and C-states, hyperthreading off on trading cores.\n\nWhich is why the measurement that matters is p99.99, not the mean. A system with a 5 us mean and a 2 ms p99.99 is UNUSABLE,\nbecause that 2 ms lands on somebody's order and costs them money. Functional determinism is correctness; latency determinism\nis the product.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d4",
   "type": "line",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1064,
   "width": 1670,
